    <h1>About this site</h1>
    <p>Deborah Daramola created this site for IT 3203. It explains how browsers request web pages, how HTTP has changed, and how HTTPS protects information in transit.</p>

    <section aria-labelledby="start-here">
      <h2 id="start-here">How to use the site</h2>
      <p>Start with <a href="concepts.html">Key Terms</a>, then read about <a href="evolution.html">HTTP history</a> and <a href="https.html">HTTPS</a>. Visit <a href="references.html">References</a> if you want to read more.</p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="quiz-guide">
      <h2 id="quiz-guide">Test what you learned</h2>
      <p>The quiz has 10 questions: two short answers, seven single-choice questions, and one select-all question. You have 10 minutes, and 7 correct answers is a passing score.</p>
      <p>When you submit or time runs out, you’ll see your score, time spent, and the correct answers. Select <strong>Retake Quiz</strong> to clear your answers and try again.</p>
      <p><a href="quiz.html">Open the quiz</a></p>
